          "text": "On admission he had a temperature of 37.6, respiratory rate of 58, mild-moderate subcostal recession, widespread fine creps and wheeze, and oxygen saturations of 90% on room air. Nasopharyngeal aspirate confirmed RSV. He was commenced on supplemental oxygen to maintain saturations ≥90% and nasogastric feeds (with IV fluids as contingency). No antibiotics were given given the viral aetiology, and salbutamol was not used as it is not indicated in bronchiolitis. By Day 2 his saturations had improved to 93–95% on room air, respiratory rate had settled to 44, recession was mild only, feeding had improved to approximately 75% orally with wet nappies returning; supplemental oxygen was weaned and the nasogastric tube was removed.",
